issue.description:
Prevent text selection highlight styling from inheriting or responding to the global Geometry radius control.

## Context

The current text selection highlight appears to become rounded when the theme radius is increased.

Observed behavior:

* with low/zero radius, selected text highlight appears sharp/rectangular;
* with larger theme radius, the selected-text highlight appears to inherit rounded corners.

This is not desirable. Text selection should remain visually crisp and rectangular regardless of the theme's component radius.

## Goal

Make text selection highlight a deliberate local exception to global radius theming.

Changing the Geometry radius control should continue to affect accepted radius-aware UI, but it should not alter the shape of selected-text highlighting.

## 1. Preserve sharp selection edges

Text selection highlight should remain square/sharp at all theme radius values.

Requirements:

* no rounded selection corners;
* no inherited radius from theme/component geometry;
* no dependence on the global radius token;
* preserve current selection foreground/background colors;
* preserve native/browser text-selection behavior.

## 2. Fix the correct source

Do not patch only the specific command/search input shown in the observed screenshot.

Inspect the implementation to determine whether the rounded selection is caused by:

* a shared `::selection` rule;
* inherited border-radius styling;
* a selection wrapper;
* component-specific styling;
* another shared theme-rendering path.

Fix the behavior at the correct shared source so equivalent text-selection surfaces remain consistent.

## 3. Scope

Audit text-selectable surfaces affected by the shared implementation, including where applicable:

* text inputs;
* search/command input;
* textareas;
* code/text preview surfaces;
* other selectable Workbench text.

Do not broaden the ticket into redesigning selection colors or input styling.

## 4. Preserve theme behavior

Do not change:

* Geometry radius behavior for normal components;
* input/container radius;
* Button radius behavior;
* card/dialog/popover radius;
* Theme v3 schema;
* color tokens;
* UI Effects;
* persistence/history;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry;
* dependencies;
* network behavior.

The only intended behavior change is selection-highlight geometry.

## 5. Accessibility / interaction

Preserve:

* native text selection;
* keyboard selection;
* mouse/pointer selection;
* focus behavior;
* selection contrast;
* selection colors in light/dark modes;
* browser editing behavior.

Do not replace native text selection with a custom selection system.

## 6. Verification

Verify at minimum:

* selected text remains rectangular at radius = 0;
* selected text remains rectangular at medium radius;
* selected text remains rectangular at high/max supported radius;
* command/search input selection is unaffected by radius;
* any other shared affected selectable surfaces remain sharp;
* selection foreground/background colors remain unchanged;
* normal component radii still respond to the Geometry radius control;
* light/dark modes remain coherent;
* no regression to keyboard/mouse text selection.

## Acceptance

* Text selection highlight no longer changes shape with the global radius control.
* Selection edges remain sharp/rectangular across supported radius values.
* The fix is applied at the correct shared source rather than as a one-off patch for a single field.
* Selection colors and native interaction behavior remain unchanged.
* Normal theme/component radius behavior remains intact.
* No Theme v3, persistence, Design Command, mutation, registry, dependency, network, or public API regression is introduced.
